<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kenneth MacAlpin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 858</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Kenneth I of Scotland, Cináed mac Ailpín</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kenneth MacAlpin was a king of Gaelic origin who became ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picts">Picts</a> around 843. Later tradition made him the founder of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, uniting the Picts with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaels">Gaels</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a>, although the merger into the kingdom of Alba took several more generations. His descendants ruled Scotland for over two centuries.</p></div>
